  "query_preview": "..\n(This evening through next Sunday)\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW: Current satellite imagery shows clear \nskies and calm conditions. This is expected to continue through \nthe work week as an exiting trough leaves zonal flow behind it. A \nwarming trend is also expected with this pattern change, with \nhighs climbing from the mid 70s today to the upper 80s by \nThursday. Overnight lows will also be at their coldest tonight \nwith lows in the upper 30s and 40s, although a few of the coldest \nvalleys may approach freezing. Widespread frost is not expected \nbut those in the usual colder locations may wish to protect any \nremaining outdoor plants. After tonight lows in the 30s are not \nexpected until potentially this weekend. Models currently show a \nstrong upper level low swinging southeast into the Pacific \nNorthwest for Saturday and Sunday. Potential impacts from this \nsystem are currently expected to be colder temperatures and \nincreased cloud cover.\n\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: High confidence in cool\ntemperatures through tomorrow and a warming trend through late\nweek. Low confidence in the weekend weather system. No changes to\nNBM output.",
